# Sprint 2 Walkthrough — Database & Alembic

We have successfully completed all Sprint 2 objectives for Aegilon XDR. Below is a summary of the achievements, configurations, and verification results.

## Changes Made

### 1. SQLAlchemy 2.0 Async Models (`app/models/`)
All core data models were implemented using SQLAlchemy 2.0's typed declarative mapping (`Mapped[]`, `mapped_column()`):
* **[User](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/app/models/user.py)**: Represents the dashboard users (admin/analyst). Defines a `relationship` to `Incident`.
* **[SecurityEvent](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/app/models/security_event.py)**: Stores raw telemetry. Defines a 1:1 `relationship` to `Alert`.
* **[Alert](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/app/models/alert.py)**: Results of anomaly detection. Connects to `SecurityEvent` and `Incident` (nullable).
* **[Incident](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/app/models/incident.py)**: Groups High/Critical alerts. Connects to `User` (assigned assignee) and `Remediation` response history.
* **[Remediation](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/app/models/remediation.py)**: Keeps track of OpenClaw automated response execution.

### 2. Centralized Model Discovery & Configuration
* **[__init__.py](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/app/models/__init__.py)**: Configured to import all models, ensuring SQLAlchemy registers metadata correctly.
* **[base.py](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/app/db/base.py)**: Acts as the single source of truth for `Base.metadata` and handles model imports to avoid circular import issues.
* **[alembic.ini](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/alembic.ini)**: Created to provide the core migration configuration (`script_location`).
* **[script.py.mako](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/alembic/script.py.mako)**: Restored to standard Alembic template.
* **[env.py](file:///c:/Users/shery/Documents/aegilon/backend/alembic/env.py)**: Configured to connect to `Base.metadata` and perform async migrations using the `asyncpg` engine.

## Verification & Testing

### 1. Database Deployment (Docker)
PostgreSQL was spun up in Docker on port `5433` (to avoid conflicts with the host Windows Postgres on `5432`):
```bash
docker compose up -d
```

### 2. Alembic Migrations
Migrations were generated and successfully applied to the Docker PostgreSQL container:
* **Generation**: `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Initial migration"`
  * Created script `alembic/versions/2ff73e32e6b7_initial_migration.py`.
* **Application**: `uv run alembic upgrade head`
  * Correctly created all database tables in PostgreSQL.

